Revoking an authorization has no effect on Personal Access Tokens, Service Access Tokens, or API and application keys. Delete or rotate those in their own management pages.

For header-based authentication, a Datadog [Personal Access Token (PAT)](https://docs.datadoghq.com/account_management/personal-access-tokens.md) or [Service Access Token (SAT)](https://docs.datadoghq.com/account_management/service-access-tokens.md) is the preferred option. Pass the token as a bearer token in the `Authorization` header. No API key is required.

### API and application keys{% #api-and-application-keys %}
Alternatively, provide a Datadog [API key and application key](https://docs.datadoghq.com/account_management/api-app-keys.md) as `DD_API_KEY` and `DD_APPLICATION_KEY` HTTP headers:
{% callout %}
# Important note for users on the following Datadog sites: app.datadoghq.com, us3.datadoghq.com, us5.datadoghq.com, app.datadoghq.eu, ap1.datadoghq.com, ap2.datadoghq.com, uk1.datadoghq.com
For example, based on your selected [Datadog site](https://docs.datadoghq.com/getting_started/site.md#navigate-the-datadog-documentation-by-site) ({% placeholder "user-datadog-site-name" /%}):
```
{
"mcpServers": {
"datadog": {
"type": "http",
"url": "<YOUR_MCP_SERVER_ENDPOINT>",
"headers": {
"DD_API_KEY": "<YOUR_API_KEY>",
"DD_APPLICATION_KEY": "<YOUR_APPLICATION_KEY>"
}
}
}
}
```
{% /callout %}
For security, use a scoped API key and application key from a [service account](https://docs.datadoghq.com/account_management/org_settings/service_accounts.md) that has only the required permissions.
**Note**: An AI client's [OAuth application scopes](https://docs.datadoghq.com/account_management/rbac/mcp_access.md#restrict-actions-for-a-specific-ai-client) do not apply to connections that use API and application keys or access tokens. These connections have the access of the key or token.
